====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} One who works with, or has an interest in, [[technology]] or [[computer]]s.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1999|author=Susan Rabin; Barbara J. Lagowski|title=Cyberflirt: how to attract anyone, anywhere on the World Wide Web
|passage=Cyberflirts are also looking for men and women who are intelligent. The internet is a '''techie''' magnet. It's only natural that those drawn to the web are also drawn to people who are quick-witted, perceptive and astute.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=30-08-2009|author=Allen Salkin|title=For Him, the Web Was No Safety Net|work=w:The New York Times|url=http://www.nytimes.com/2009/08/30/fashion/30harris.html
|passage=He began giving parties in a loft on Broadway at Houston Street, with artists, '''techies''' and other downtowners.}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} A person who works on the technical side of events.

